# AM01 Touch Screen UI Configuration
#
# Read by odo-ui.service.
#
# odo-ui takes ONE optional argument: the path to status.json. It does NOT
# accept -fb or -touch -- an earlier version of this file passed those, which
# would have made odo-ui treat "-fb" as the status path and fail. The
# framebuffer is hardcoded to /dev/fb0 and the touch device is discovered by
# scanning /dev/input/event*.
#
# REQUIREMENTS:
#   - A real Linux framebuffer at /dev/fb0. odo-ui uses the FBIOGET_*SCREENINFO
#     ioctls and mmaps it, so it needs a genuine fbdev -- on this board that
#     means HDMI. An SPI panel would need a kernel framebuffer driver first.
#   - A touch device under /dev/input/ (USB, or via a driver).
#
# With no framebuffer the unit is skipped, not failed. Use odo-webd instead.
UI_OPTS="/run/odod/status.json"
